        The control is EXPECTED to fail: with no --host-dlopen its dlopen
        reaches the host loader, which is experiments/50-'s result. Its count
        is recorded, never asserted, because what it does is host-dependent.
        
        The musl rows of the NATIVE arm are a refusal by design: a host object
        there needs musl's libc, and mapping it into a glibc image is the
        second-libc outcome docs/limitations.md §1 calls worse than failing.
        
        ⭐ BIGTLS is TODO T-072's subject and the pair is the measurement.
        56,248 bytes of INITIAL-EXEC thread-local storage against glibc's
        ~3,168 bytes of surplus headroom -- a surplus that does NOT grow with
        the program, which route B measured and refuted. Reserve 0 must
        REFUSE and say so through dlerror(); 65536 must load it. A refusal
        that arrived as a SIGNAL would be the loader failing, not declining,
        so exit* is counted and SIG* is not.
        
        size cost of --tls-reserve 65536 on the binary: 80 bytes

